## Why divergence clustering matters more than the rate

92% agreement clustered on one exception type is a **fixable gap** — a missing rule, probably already in the exception register, possibly a day's work.

92% scattered randomly is a **capability ceiling** — no amount of iteration will move it.

These look identical in a summary metric and require completely different decisions. Always categorise before reporting.

